{"violation_type":{"id":"tx-tac-746-1801-a","jurisdiction":"TX","state":"TX","code_system":"Texas Administrative Code, Title 26, Ch. 746","original_code":"746.1801(a)","title":"Child/Caregiver Ratio for Field Trips - Areas Open to General Public (26 TAC §746.1801(a))","short_title":"Child/Caregiver Ratio for Field Trips - Areas Open to General Public","severities":{"medium_high":15},"facility_ids":["tx-hhsc-1470878","tx-hhsc-123425","tx-hhsc-1337465","tx-hhsc-610528","tx-hhsc-354788","tx-hhsc-95152","tx-hhsc-1237531","tx-hhsc-1293691","tx-hhsc-856370","tx-hhsc-116984","tx-hhsc-971548","tx-hhsc-1251597","tx-hhsc-1305395","tx-hhsc-574488","tx-hhsc-159804"],"first_date":"2022-07-06","last_date":"2026-06-01","typical_finding":"It was determined a class of 8 children and 1 caregiver took a walking field trip to a public pond and there were other instances where the caregiver had 12 children and 1 caregiver walking to the pond.","finding_variants":[{"text":"It was determined a class of 8 children and 1 caregiver took a walking field trip to a public pond and there were other instances where the caregiver had 12 children and 1 caregiver walking to the pond.","count":1},{"text":"During the inspection, it was observed a group of 20 children went on a field trip to the library with 3 caregivers. Field trips ratios indicate that 4 caregivers were required. This was corrected when they returned to the center.","count":1},{"text":"The field trip group was out of ratio on a field trip that required the ratio to be 1 caregiver for 12 children with the youngest child being 6 years of age and older.  The caregiver was supervising 14 children.","count":1},{"text":"Based on the age of the youngest child in the group, the ratio of children to adults on a field trip to an area that was open to the general public was not followed.","count":1},{"text":"During a DFPS investigation, it was determined that the operation was out of ratio during a field trip.  There were children ranging in ag